.TH PYTHON-TEMPLATE 1 "" "python-template" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
python-template \- an example command: a pet you can feed and play with
.SH SYNOPSIS
.RS 4
.nf
python\-template [\-\-version] [command] [options]
python\-template status [\-\-name NAME] [\-\-json]
python\-template feed [\-\-times N] [\-\-name NAME] [\-\-json]
python\-template play [\-\-times N] [\-\-name NAME] [\-\-json]
python\-template guide
python\-template man [\-\-install | \-\-raw]
.fi
.RE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBpython\-template\fR is the example command that ships with python-package-template. It keeps a pet whose state is two numbers from 0 to 10: hunger, where 0 is full, and happiness, where 10 is happy. It exists to show the conventions a command made from the template follows, so replace it with your own once you have renamed the package.
.PP
The conventions: every command prints a sentence for people and JSON with \fB\-\-json\fR; \fBguide\fR prints this manual for people and agents alike; \fBman\fR shows the same text as a man page; exit status 0 means success.
.PP
With no command, \fBpython\-template\fR runs \fBstatus\fR.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBstatus\fR
Show the pet as it starts: hunger 5, happiness 5.
.TP
\fBfeed\fR
Lower hunger by one per feed, never below 0, then show the pet.
.TP
\fBplay\fR
Raise happiness by one per game, never above 10, then show the pet.
.TP
\fBguide\fR
Print this manual as Markdown.
.TP
\fBman\fR
Show the man page. \fB\-\-install\fR puts it where \fBman python\-template\fR finds it; \fB\-\-raw\fR prints roff.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-name NAME\fR
The pet's name. Default: Baby Python.
.TP
\fB\-\-times N\fR
How many times to feed or play, 1 to 10. Default: 1.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print one JSON object instead of a sentence.
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
Print the version and exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Print the options of a command and exit.
.SH JSON OUTPUT
.PP
\fBstatus\fR, \fBfeed\fR and \fBplay\fR print one object with three fields:
.RS 4
.nf
{"name": "Baby Python", "hunger": 4, "happiness": 5}
.fi
.RE
.PP
\fBname\fR is a string; \fBhunger\fR and \fBhappiness\fR are integers from 0 to 10.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.PP
0 on success. 2 when the arguments are wrong, with the reason on standard error.
.SH FILES
.PP
\fB~/.local/share/man/man1/python\-template.1\fR is where \fBman \-\-install\fR writes the man page, or \fB$XDG_DATA_HOME/man/man1/\fR when that variable is set.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Feed the pet three times and read the result as JSON:
.RS 4
.nf
python\-template feed \-\-times 3 \-\-json
.fi
.RE
.PP
Install the man page, then read it:
.RS 4
.nf
python\-template man \-\-install
man python\-template
.fi
.RE
.SH FOR AGENTS
.PP
Run commands with \fB\-\-json\fR and parse the object; the fields are stable. \fBpython\-template guide\fR returns this whole manual, so an agent can learn the command without browsing. Nothing here touches the network or the disk, except \fBman \-\-install\fR, which writes one file in the user's man folder.
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
The template and its checks: https://github.com/jpsanders/python-package-template
.SH AUTHOR
.PP
James Phillip Sanders, https://jamesphillipsanders.com
